A||||18||Adrift||DO NOT buy a kit car from Tony Sousa!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||12-05-2001||05:36 PM||||I thought I'd open this forum by warning you all of the terrible service and support I recieved from Tony Sousa. <BR>What attracted me to him first was his cheap prices on Kits, as well as his "honesty" - he didn't ask for  money until he actually delievered the kit. I found him so honest in fact that I decided to by my Fiero donor from him. Boy, did I make a mistake...<P>First of all, the kit took about triple the amount of time he told me it would be delievered in. So we begin with a delivery which was about one month late. First rule about Tony: He is INCREDIBLY UNRELIABLE. When the Kit arrived I payed him, yet later found out that he had forgot to bring the lights with him that I also was going to pay for. He said he would get someone to drop them off in the next three days. I called him multiple times, he said he would drop them off, I stayed home waiting for him, he never showed up. About a week and a half later he showed up to drop them off (About 8 hours later then he said he would, showed up at my door at 10:30 instead of 3:00). He said at this time it would take another two months for my car to be ready - it took three.<P>The fibreglass quality was actually pretty bad - there were no holes in the body for mounting, which made just getting the body onto the car more then a day job. There were also air bubbles throughout the body, which made it sit improperly. On top of this Tony had done a faulty welding job and didn't put the front clip support on right - this resulted in the hood not sitting correctly. There were also cracks and dents through the body, as well as seems still visible (and pertruding) in some parts of the fibreglass.<P>When the car was completed (one month late) I got a bill for more then I expected - what tony decided to do was buy two junked cars for $300 each (Something which he mentioned to me casually in one of our discussions) and then sell me EACH piece of the car seperatly! In the end it cost me about $3000 for the car. On top of this, he asked me for $300 after the fact which I believed was for the brake parts which he had ordered for me (Or was supposed to!). Turns out it wasn't, it was for the battery and engine belts in my car (both used)! He never even bothered ordering any of the brake parts, and still hasn't (four months later).<P>Let me also remind you at this point that Tony doesn't never returned any of my calls, and allows his voice mail to fill up so you can not even leave messaeges. I've gone a period of over a week without being able to contact him. <P>So where was I? Oh yes, He dropped of the car 30 days late. by the way he didn't bother hooking up the rear brakes, saying that he thought I was just going to put on new parts (which I was going to do - if he had every actually ordered the parts! Its funny how when it involves him doing more work he remebers all of a sudden that I am upgrading my brakes..) which resulted the car being put on a flatbed, another $200. The car also didn't have any interior in it at all when it arrvied, he said he would deliever it the next day. The car wouldn't start when he delievered it - the battery cables were corroded away. When it did start, it began idling at 3000 RPM. He said he'd get a mechanic down within a week to fix it. Two months later, still no mechanic (although I've called at least 4 times a week to remind him).<P>He never showed up the day after he dropped of the car to deleiver the interior parts. Or the following day. or the following day (he said every single day he would, never once did he). About FOURTEEN days later he shows up with half of the interior parts. I ask him for the other half, he says he'll drop them off the next day. Two months later, he still has never shown up. <P>I offered to drive to his place to pick them up. We made a date, i drove up (40 min drive), he wasn't there. Killed an hour till he showed up, and he diodn't have the parts. Said he'd drop them off the next day.<P>He didn't show up. or the next day. or the next.<P>Two weeks later - I call him, threatening with a lawyer - he returns my call for the first time in 120 Days, says he'll be there tomorrow. I call him the next day, he says he'll be there that night. He never shows. Never calls back...<P>A lot more happened inbetween these events - in my cellphone call record I have at least 60 calls to him, and I can only recount actually speaking to him a handful of times. <P>I have NEVER IN MY LIFE dealt with a person in business as irresponsible as Tony Sousa. All I can say it Avoid This person at all cost. It IS NOT WORTH THE MONEY YOU SAVE, because in the long run, it actually costs you more. If I were you I would avoid this manufacturer at all costs.||||reg||1
